      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Any Grid",
      "links": [],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Random\nGrids",
      "links": [],
      "level": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The arbitrary grid, chosen at random\nfrom the set of all grids, functions as a symbol: it represents\nthe whole set of possibilities. But it also demonstrates the equivalence\nof all these possibilities: the image displayed by the randomly\nsampled pixel configuration is noise. (If the resolution\nis high enough, the random grid turns into a grey or brown monochrome.)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Jean Arp",
      "links": [],
      "level": 5
    },
